; rootmotion.eval - how far a monster's body strays from where the game put it.
;
; The skeleton kit's Mixamo clips carry ROOT MOTION: a walk carries the hips
; ~0.77 units forward per cycle, a death up to ~0.6 to one side. The world moves
; a monster itself, so a clip that travelled too slid the body ahead of its
; square and snapped it back every loop (measured before the fix: `root` climbed
; 0.03 -> 0.755 over a walk__walking cycle, then dropped to 0.014).
; Animator::LockRootTravel takes the drift out of loops and holds a one-shot to
; DungeonWorld::kMonsterRootReach (0.08). `monsters` prints, per monster, the
; clip and `root` - the rig root's horizontal distance from its rest, in model
; units - which is that stray.
;
; The monster is FROZEN through its spawn clip (up to 14 s, and it glides while
; it plays, so no walk would be seen) and then let go at distance 7, which it
; notices. The death is a burn: dealt through the pipeline, and its plume rides
; the root joint, so a body that strays drags the fire with it.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 11
arena open 9 9
tp 14 16
face n
freeze on
spawn skel_warrior 14 9 s
step 16
freeze off
echo --- walk ---
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
step 0.1
monsters
echo --- death ---
freeze on
effect burn ahead 200 5
step 0.2
monsters
